 "provenance": "Angkor 12 (secret stage, world 0 level 11) secret exit 35,25, control-only on the exact S700 core. Start values: weaponTier 1 (hammer from Angkor 4; the README default for Angkor secret stages, which are reached later in the campaign; the hammer is needed for the one action at tick 813, the hook is not because no riddle room is solved and no key is used), maxHealth 4, lives 12, diamonds 82 / redDiamonds 10 (campaign totals as in the old Angkor 12/13 routes; they do not affect this route). Magic diamond lock: info.ts lists a lock at 34,25 needing 30 diamonds, but it gates nothing here. The map scan (method_304, s700.ts case 12 / cGame.java ~11870: field_334[x][y] = -1) already clears that tile at stage load, so tile(34,25) is -1 from tick 0, and nothing reads field_156 to block movement; method_352 clearing the tile again when field_156 reaches 0 (tick 202) changes nothing (forcing field_156 to stay above 0 still ends in secret-exit at tick 989). Route: from the entrance checkpoint 3,27, 35 cell moves found by beam search (a12-beam.ts) collect 30 of the 33 diamonds of the grass field (climbing each diamond stack from below and stepping aside before the stone above falls; 30th diamond at tick 202, hp 4). These diamonds are collected incidentally: they are not needed to open the way to the exit or to cross the field (from the same start, t R 9; t U 12; t R; g 14,11 reaches checkpoint 14,11 at t=148 with 0 diamonds). Then up column 7 to 7,15 -> east along row 15 to 14,15 -> up column 14 through checkpoint 14,11 (t=301..305) to 14,6 -> east along the row-6 corridor through riddle room 1 (its trigger 17,6 fires and vanishes during an 89-tick wait; riddle not solved, no keys) -> down column 26 -> checkpoint 27,11 (t=505) -> down column 28 (one hit at 28,12, t=512, hp 4->3, beside the tile-23 wall objects of column 31) -> west along row 18 over the room-3 trigger 24,18 (one snake hit at t=700, hp 3->2; snakes at 20/21,17) -> down column 16 -> checkpoint 17,22 (t=762) -> 18,26 -> 19,27. Bottom stone pocket: step through the grass at 21,27 and 22,27; standing at 22,27, one hammer action with no direction held (tick 813) cuts the grass at 23,27 (tile 10 -> stone at tick 817 as the column-23 stone stack drops one cell). That single stone is then pushed east twice: 23,27 -> 24,27 with the hero moving from 22,27 to 23,27 (t=831), and 24,27 -> 25,27 with the hero moving to 24,27 (t=842). No stone at 22,27 is pushed. Then up through the grass at 24,26 (t=847) -> 23,26 -> up 23,25..23,23 -> east along row 23 to 32,23 -> down 32,24, 32,25 -> east along row 25 over the already open cell 34,25 -> secret exit 35,25 (t=937); the exit walk ends at 52,25 (secret-exit, 989 ticks, hp 2, lives 12, 30 diamonds).",
